.TH "cbor::item_size" "3" "November 02, 2026" "mbedded-cbor 0.9.0" "mbedded-cbor"
.SH NAME
cbor::item_size \- Return the encoded size of the first CBOR data item.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \f[B]<cbor/cbor.hpp>\f[R]

\f[B]namespace\f[R] cbor {
std::expected< std::size_t, error > item_size(std::string_view const encoded);
}
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
The item must be well\-formed.
Bytes after it are ignored.
This function does not check nesting depth, UTF\-8, tag content, or
duplicate map keys.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]encoded\f[R]: Bytes that begin with the item.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The item\(cqs size in bytes, or an error if it is incomplete, malformed,
indefinite\-length, or exceeds an active size limit.
.SH ERRORS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]too_little_data\f[R]: input ends before the item or its claimed
children.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]syntax_error\f[R]: an invalid head or reserved simple value.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]indefinite_length\f[R]: a head uses indefinite length.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]string_length_exceeded\f[R]: a string exceeds an active limit.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]container_elements_exceeded\f[R]: a container exceeds an active
limit.
.SH NOTES
O(i), where i is the number of item heads examined, bounded by O(n) for
n bytes in the item.
Uses O(1) auxiliary memory and allocates nothing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// bytes: [1, 2] followed by 7, 4 bytes\f[R]
cbor::item_size(bytes);                    \f[I]// 3\f[R]
cbor::item_size(bytes.substr(0, 2));       \f[I]// too_little_data\f[R]
\f[I]// bytes: [_ 1]\f[R]
cbor::item_size(bytes);                    \f[I]// indefinite_length\f[R]
.EE
